-- =============================================================================
-- Metadata Sync — v5.34.0 release
-- =============================================================================
--
-- Generated by `mj sync push` against a clean database built to the 5.34.0 state
-- (MJ core migrations + every bizapps-common migration through V202608132240),
-- per metadata/CLAUDE.md §1b "Release-Time Metadata Sync". The push emitted
-- metadata/sql_logging/MetadataSync_Push_2026-08-14T05-54-49-219Z.sql; this file
-- is that output with its schema references corrected (see NOTE below).
--
-- WHAT THIS CARRIES. Two records changed between the JSON in metadata/ and a
-- database built purely from migrations:
--
--   1. MJ_BizApps_Common: Address Types — "Mailing".
--      IconClass moves 'fa-solid fa-mailbox' -> 'fa-solid fa-envelope'.
--      fa-mailbox is a Font Awesome PRO glyph; the bundled set is Free, so the
--      browser matched no rule and rendered an empty square. The fix landed in
--      metadata/address-types/.address-types.json, but the row itself is seeded
--      by V202605141122__v5.29.x__Metadata_Sync.sql, so without this migration
--      no database — existing OR freshly installed — would ever pick it up.
--
--   2. MJ: Schema Info for __mj_BizAppsCommon — re-asserts the registered
--      description and entity-name prefix.
--
-- NOTE ON SCHEMA REFERENCES. The emitted SQL wrote the SchemaInfo call as
-- [${flyway:defaultSchema}].spUpdateSchemaInfo. That is wrong for an Open App:
-- `mj migrate --schema __mj_BizAppsCommon` binds flyway:defaultSchema to THIS
-- app's schema, and spUpdateSchemaInfo is a CORE procedure that exists only in
-- __mj — verified against the build database, where
-- OBJECT_ID('__mj_BizAppsCommon.spUpdateSchemaInfo') is NULL. Applied verbatim
-- it would fail on the first statement. Core procedures therefore use
-- ${mjSchema}, and this app's own procedures use ${flyway:defaultSchema},
-- matching V202608132239 and the mapping declared in mj.config.cjs.
-- =============================================================================

-- Save MJ: Schema Info (core SP call only)
